2.4 Population distribution 
 
The population size of the different districts ranked by population size is displayed in Figure 4.  
 
Location had the largest population size of 1,497 people which includes 15% of the total Nauru 
population. It was followed by Meneng (1,380), and Aiwo (1,220). The districts of Ijuw and Anibare were 
the smallest districts with only 178 and 226 people, representing only 2% of the total population each 
(Fig.5).  
 
While the ranking of districts changed little during the last 19 years, the district of Location lost a lot of 
people because of the repatriation back home of the I -Kiribati and Tuvaluan workers who used to live 
there. The districts with the strongest growth were the district of Aiwo and Anabar; both grew in 
population size by 40% since 1992 (Fig.6). 
 
