2.6 Population structure 
 
The enumerated 2011 resident population consisted of 5,105 males and 4,979 females. Males out -
numbered females by 126 resulting in a sex ratio of 103, which means that there were 103 males per 100 
females. However, the sex ratio declined continuously since 1992 when there were 105 males per 100 
females (Table 2, Fig.8, and App.1).  
 
