fertility decline is apparent a s the average number of  live-births per woman, especially for women aged 
30 years and older, declined from one census to the next. While th e average number of live-births per 
women aged 45-49 years was 5.2 in 1992, it declined to 4.6 and 4.0 in 2002 and 2011. 
  
