15 and Fig.29), indicating earlier death of male spouses. 
 
Life expectancies for males and females in the Nauru compare with 78.8 and 82.7 years for males and 
females in New Zealand , and in Australia it is 79.3 and 83.9 years. Therefore an average person in New 
Zealand or Australia lives about 20 years longer than a Nauruan (Fig.35). 
 
Nauru‘s life expectancy is one of the lowest of all Pacific Island Countries and Territories (PICT). 
 
 
