This included 78 people, and of those 33 people were recorded as lame, and another 30 people were mute, 
24 people were blind, 19 mentally disabled, 1 5 could not grasp, and 13 were deaf (please note that a 
person can have more than one disability). 
 
Nine people with a severe disability – 7 males and 2 females - were enrolled in school, and another 8 (7 
males and 1 female) were employed for wages or salary. 
 
