4.8.4 Employment status 
 
Out of a total of 2,883 people in paid employment, about 93 % (2,669) were employees either with a 
private enterprise or as government workers. Only abo ut 5% were self employed (158 ), and a to tal of 25 
people were employers. The proportion of males and females in the different employment categories were 
very similar (Fig.69). 
 
More than two-third of the population in paid employment worked 36 hours per we ek or more, and about 
20% worked 20 hours or less. The average number of hours  worked per week was about 32.5 hours, and 
there was no significant difference in hours worked between males and females (Fig.70). 
 
