5.4 Household income sources 
 
5.4.1 Main household income 
 
During the last 3 months before the  2011 census, 85% of households recorded wages or salary  as their 
main source of household income, 7% of households main income came from own business activities, 4% 
relied on rent of land, and 2% on the sale of fish, crops or handicrafts. Another 1% of households reported 
that income from remittances or from renting a house was their main source of income (Fig.77). 
 
There was a slight variation in the importance of the different household income sources by district, and 
the proportion of households with wages or salary as the main source of income was lowest in 
Denigomodu (76%), Yaren (78%), and Location (85%). Here income from own businesses was relatively 
more important than in the other districts. 
 
